^SAMPLE = GSM3611452
!Sample_title = DMSO treatment
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM3611452
!Sample_status = Public on Mar 04 2019
!Sample_submission_date = Feb 18 2019
!Sample_last_update_date = Mar 04 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = DMSO treatment
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: 786-O
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: clear-cell carcinoma
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Prior to screening, the viral titer and volume was pre-determined with pilot experiments to ensure about 30% infection rate in the screening experiment and caution was taken to minimize multiple constructs transduced into the same cell. Optimized surface area for cell growth was pre-determined in pilot experiments to avoid over confluence during screening. Puromycin concentrations were pre-determined with pilot experiments before the screen. For the screening experiment, 150 million 786-O-Cas9 cells were infected with a lentiviral library containing 77,441 sgRNA targeting 18,000 genes in the human genome to ensure each sgRNA is represented by at least 500 cells on average47. For the infection, cells added with the calculated lentivirus volume were supplemented with 4mg/mL of polybrene and centrifuged at 950xg for 2 hours. Fresh media was added at a 1:1 ratio post-centrifugation. Infected cells were selected with 2mg/mL of puromycin for 96 hours, expanded for another 4 days to reach the desired cell number and split for DMSO or 5mM ML210 treatment. At least 40 million cells were used for each treatment condition to keep the minimum presentation number for each sgRNA above 500. Cells were exposed to ML210 treatment for 4, 6, or 8 days before being cultured in drug-free media for recovery and expansion for 24h.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = 786-O cells were cultured in RPMI-1640 (Gibco) media supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum (Gibco) and 1% penicillin/streptomycin in a humidified incubator at 37°C with 5% CO2.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA from cell pellets was purified using the QIAamp DNA Blood Maxi/Midi/Mini kits (Qiagen) according to the manufacturer’s protocols and quantified using a Nanodrop 2000 (Thermo Fisher Scientific).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = sgRNA cassettes were PCR-amplified and barcoded with sequencing adaptors utilizing ExTaq DNA Polymerase (Clontech). PCR products were purified with Agencourt AMPure XP SPRI beads (Beckman Coulter A63880) according to the manufacturer’s instructions, quantified using a Nanodrop 2000, pooled into a master sequencing pool, and sequenced on a MiSeq sequencer (Illumina) with 300nt single-end reads, loaded at 60% with a 5% spike-in of PhiX DNA.
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR screen
!Sample_data_processing = raw data includes sequencing reads for the sgRNAs in the library
!Sample_data_processing = Sequence mapping and counting: For CRISPR screen data analysis, the sgRNA sequences were mapped to a reference file containing all SpCas9 sgRNAs in the library and the sgRNA-associated barcodes were counted and mapped to the barcode reference file. The reference file containing all the sgRNAs in the Brunello library is included in this submission, and can be found publicly at https://media.addgene.org/cms/filer_public/8b/4c/8b4c89d9-eac1-44b2-bb2f-8fea95672705/broadgpp-brunello-library-contents.txt .
!Sample_data_processing = Read count normalization: The read count matrix was normalized to reads per million reads (RPM) within each condition.
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: The read count matrix is presented as a txt file.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL16791
!Sample_contact_name = Yilong,,Zou
!Sample_contact_email = zouyilong@westlake.edu.cn
!Sample_contact_laboratory = Laboratory of Functional Lipidomics and Metabolic Regulation
!Sample_contact_department = School of Life Sciences
!Sample_contact_institute = Westlake University
!Sample_contact_address = Shilongshan Road #18, Cloud Town, Xihu District
!Sample_contact_city = Hangzhou
!Sample_contact_state = Zhejiang
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 310024
!Sample_contact_country = China
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina HiSeq 2500
!Sample_library_selection = other
!Sample_library_source = genomic
!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN10962533
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX5388233
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE
!Sample_series_id = GSE126696
!Sample_data_row_count = 0
